# Public release notes

When preparing a public release description, keep the changelog concise and user-focused. Summarize what changed and why it matters; omit implementation details such as precise frequencies and timings unless users need them. Preserve important compatibility, migration, platform, and validation limitations, and do not overstate fidelity.

Detailed technical release notes and documentation in the repository may remain detailed.
